Z||000013||Fformula88||10-11-2000||08:09 PM||||Welcome to the site FieroGrrrl!  <P>19 MPG isn't all that low for the Fiero's V6 in city driving.  It could be any number of things.  My Formula gets about 21 MPG in mostly city driving with some short highway stints.  <P>Good luck with your repairs!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/fierosig1.jpg">   <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<p>[This message has been edited by Fformula88 (edited 10-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||BAM-BAM||10-11-2000||08:20 PM||||   FGRRRL, I wouldn't worry about the CV joint it's really pretty simple. I don't consider myself to be much of a mechanic and I was scared at first. As the process progressed it became very simple. Just be sure and clean everything good. I even took the spider gear bearings out and reassembled them. It was more intemidating than it should have been.<P>  Later, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
Z||000015||sdm1964||10-11-2000||10:11 PM||||Welcome, Jeff told me he sent you here. Always good to have another fiero fanatic. Can't wait to see some pics of the car. Can you make the car show in Daytona in March? So many fieros and so little time.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Babygirl||10-11-2000||10:31 PM||||Welcome to the Forum!  IT's nice to see another female who loves her Fiero!  As for the miles per gallon, I hate to top ya, but I get anywhere from 25-29 per gallon.  THen again, I only use Supreme gas in my baby!!.  <P>------------------<BR>~Darcy & Laura<BR>1984 Black SE Fiero||||reg||6
Z||000017||FieroGrrrl||10-13-2000||04:32 AM||||Wow, thanks for the energetic welcome!  I tend to take a little while to come back and check up, I work nights, so if I take a while to respond, forgive me!!!!<P>Okay as for the MPG, I used to get 32 MPG, but California likes to add funky things to their gas that is entirely too toxic, but somehow good for the "environment".  Don't get me wrong, I'm all for saving the planet, but Christ leave my CAR alone!!!  Add that to the INSANE smog requirements and fuel efficiancy is usually seriously affected.  Still I was getting like 26-29 after the gas change.  It's all very recent, my idle air control is busted, I think that has something to do with it, but I *can't* figure out what else it could possibly be!  Oh and my baby ONLY gets Shell 92 or Chevron 92, which is like $2.25 a gallon in the bay area, so as you can imagine I'm putting like $70.00 in the tank every week.  I don't know, she just seems sick...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I guess the worst problem is that not only is my new IAC sitting in the glove flap, but the ultimate dog bone is on my passenger side floorboards, I'VE BEEN BUSY!!!<P>Okay, enough self-defense!  I will try to get a picture of at least Perceus on the site, I have to get my roomate to get the digital camera out and then you can all "ooh and ahh" over my precious little baby  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Oh, and girls, definetly!!!  There simply aren't enough of us who actually work on our own cars!  I think it is the most relaxing thing I do with my weekends!  I get more phone numbers that way.....<P>Hmmmm, <P>Always,<BR>~Fierogrrrl<P>aka Christine<P><BR>Hi Jeff!||||reg||10
Z||000018||2xsess||10-13-2000||08:16 PM||||My 85Gt only gets about 15mpg city. And I only run high test in it. <P>The ultimate dogbone is a great buy, I put one in mine only a week after I bought it and that engine doesn't move!!!<P>I do believe the IAC sitting in the glove flap isn't a good thing at all.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
